<html>
<head>
<title>Help</title>
</head>
<body>
<br>

<h4>Results</h4>

<h4><b>Results Table - Prophylactic Vaccination</b></h4>
<p>The main results table shows prophylactic vaccination requirements for each selected country, species, and year. The information includes:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Population</strong>: Total livestock head count for the selected country, species, and year</li>
<li><strong>Prophylactic Vaccination (doses)</strong>: Total number of vaccine doses required</li>
<li><strong>Youngstock Vaccination (doses)</strong>: Vaccine doses needed for young animals</li>
<li><strong>Adult Vaccination (doses)</strong>: Vaccine doses needed for adult animals</li>
<li><strong>Proportion and Coverage</strong>: Percentages used in calculations</li>
</ul>

<h4><b>Map View - Regional Distribution</b></h4>
<p>After reviewing the prophylactic vaccination requirements, click the <strong>"See/Update Map"</strong> button to view regional distribution. This step is essential for seeing emergency vaccination needs.</p>

<p>The map shows:</p>
<ul>
<li>Color-coded regions based on livestock density</li>
<li>Detailed information for each administrative region</li>
<li>Regional vaccine needs for both prophylactic and emergency vaccination</li>
</ul>

<h4><b>Emergency Vaccination</b></h4>
<p>Emergency vaccination requirements are only visible after clicking the "See/Update Map" button. The calculation is based on:</p>
<ul>
<li>The ring vaccination radius you selected (determining the area covered)</li>
<li>Livestock density in each administrative region</li>
<li>The proportions and coverage settings from your parameters</li>
</ul>
<p>The emergency vaccination figure represents doses needed for <strong>a single outbreak</strong>. For multiple outbreaks, multiply this number by your expected outbreak count.</p>

<h4><b>Regional Details</b></h4>
<p>When you click on any region in the map, a detailed information table appears showing:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Country</strong>: The country selected</li>
<li><strong>Species</strong>: The livestock species</li>
<li><strong>ADM1_Name</strong>: The administrative region name</li>
<li><strong>Density</strong>: Percentage of the country's total population for this species in this region</li>
<li><strong>Head_km²</strong>: Livestock density (animals per square kilometer)</li>
<li><strong>Prophylactic Vaccination (doses)</strong>: Required doses by year for systematic vaccination</li>
<li><strong>Emergency Vaccination (doses)</strong>: Required doses by year for emergency response</li>
</ul>

<h4><b>Full Table View</b></h4>
<p>Click the <strong>"See/Update Full Table"</strong> button below the map to view comprehensive data for all administrative regions. This consolidated table:</p>
<ul>
<li>Shows all regions across selected countries</li>
<li>Displays vaccination needs for all selected years in a single row per region</li>
<li>Can be downloaded using the buttons at the top</li>
<li>Includes search functionality to locate specific regions or data points</li>
</ul>

